# Cybernetics and Education (Special Issue)

**Authors:** Kopstein, Felix F., Ed.

## Abstract
This is a special issue examining the potential of cybernetics in educational technology. Articles discuss: cybernetic methods, algorithms, feedback learning theory, a structural approach to behavioral objectives and criterion-referenced testing, task specifications and diagnosis, teacher-child interaction, educational development, teaching machines, the "talking typewriter," and a model for improving instruction in the U.S. Marine Corps. (DAG)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ173955

